      "content": "It’s true that if multiple countries adopt protectionist policies, it generally hinders the progress made towards a more interconnected and efficient global economy. Over the long run, such policies increase volatility and can lead to a less efficient allocation of resources. Tariffs and trade barriers typically result in higher costs for consumers and businesses, which can stifle innovation and reduce economic growth. Furthermore, protectionism can provoke trade wars and retaliation between countries, potentially causing widespread economic disruption and instability. It also undermines the benefits of free trade, such as specialization and comparative advantage, which are thought to contribute to increased productivity and economic prosperity in the global marketplace.",
